Apple will face trial in France in June 2027 over allegations that it restricted independent iPhone repairs, French advocacy group Halte à l'Obsolescence Programmée (HOP) this week <a href="https://www.halteobsolescence.org/annonce-proces-apple-2027/">announced</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/11/iPhone-Self-Service-Repair.jpg" alt="" width="1960" height="1102" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-976474" /><br/>
The case follows HOP's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2023/05/15/france-investigating-apple-planned-obsolescence/">December 2022 complaint</a> about parts pairing, which electronically links components to a specific iPhone. The group says that Apple's restrictions caused replacement screens, batteries, and cameras to malfunction when repairs were performed outside its approved channels, even when genuine Apple parts were used.<br/>
<br/>
According to HOP's <a href="https://www.halteobsolescence.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Dossier-de-presse-proces-Apple-2-FR-6.pdf">press materials</a>, the complaint covers 24 iPhone models and practices between November 2021 and July 2024. Although HOP describes the case as involving planned obsolescence, the specific offense being prosecuted is obstructing repair and refurbishment under French consumer law.<br/>
<br/>
Apple denied the allegations in a statement to <a href="https://www.lemonde.fr/en/pixels/article/2026/11/17/apple-to-face-trial-in-france-over-planned-obsolescence_6782735_13.html"><em>Le Monde</em></a>, calling them baseless. It also highlighted restrictions it has lifted, including allowing <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/06/26/iphone-third-party-display-battery-support/">True Tone to work</a> with third-party replacement displays.<br/>
<br/>
Since the complaint was initiated, Apple has <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2024/04/11/apple-to-allow-used-parts-for-repairs/">expanded support for used genuine parts</a>, initially for iPhone 15 models and newer. Apple <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2024/04/apple-to-expand-repair-options-with-support-for-used-genuine-parts/">says parts pairing</a> protects privacy, security, and safety. HOP acknowledges the changes, but says their effectiveness needs to be assessed over time.<br/>
<br/>
